# Triad Arpeggios in First Position (repertoire plan: st-arpeggio-triads). An original study in
# C major, eighth notes, alternate picking (down on the beat, up on the "and").
# Bars 1-12: the six major and minor chords of C major climb one step at a time, two bars each,
# every arpeggio one octave up and down from its root (root, third, fifth, octave), landing on the
# root as a half note. B diminished waits for the seventh-chord study.
#   C   C E G C   string 5 fret 3, string 4 fret 2, string 3 open, string 2 fret 1 (the C shape)
#   Dm  D F A D   string 4 open, string 4 fret 3, string 3 fret 2, string 2 fret 3 (finger 4)
#   Em  E G B E   string 4 fret 2, strings 3, 2 and 1 open
#   F   F A C F   string 4 fret 3, string 3 fret 2, string 2 fret 1, string 1 fret 1 (the small F)
#   G   G B D G   string 6 fret 3, string 5 fret 2, strings 4 and 3 open (the bottom of G)
#   Am  A C E A   string 5 open, string 5 fret 3 (finger 4), string 4 fret 2, string 3 fret 2
# Bars 13-16: a short tune made of the same arpeggios, two chords a bar (F G | Em Am | Dm G | C).
# The top note of each group sings a slow line on its own: C D | E C | D B | C.
title: Triad Arpeggios in First Position
